sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  actor PT as Patient
  participant DEV as BP cuff<br/>(Bluetooth)
  participant LAPP as Luscii app
  participant LUS as Luscii Clinical Engine<br/>(Class IIa)
  participant LUI as Luscii integration layer
  participant CORE as Core service
  participant BUS as Event bus
  participant EHRI as EHR integration layer
  participant HIX as Chipsoft HiX
  participant NOT as Notification subsystem
  actor CL as ZAS clinician

  Note over PT,CL: Daily RPM measurement → threshold breach → clinical alert → task in HiX<br/>This flow stays inside the CE Class IIa boundary up to the point of clinician task creation.

  rect rgb(225, 240, 225)
  Note right of LUS: ━━ CE Class IIa boundary ━━<br/>(Luscii regulated zone)

  PT->>DEV: Take blood-pressure reading
  DEV->>LAPP: BLE: pair + transmit reading<br/>(SBP, DBP, HR, timestamp)
  LAPP->>LUS: POST measurement<br/>(internal Luscii API)

  LUS->>LUS: Validate against Instrument<br/>(SNOMED-CT coded type)<br/>Apply threshold + trend rules<br/>(from active Program)

  alt Reading within thresholds
    LUS-->>LAPP: Acknowledge<br/>(no alert generated)
    LAPP-->>PT: Confirmation + next-step guidance
  else Threshold breach detected
    LUS->>LUS: Generate Alert<br/>(priority: high/medium/low)<br/>Project to FHIR Flag
  end
  end

  Note over LUS,CORE: Boundary crossing — Class IIa output (Flag) leaves Luscii<br/>via FHIR Webhook to the Luscii integration layer.

  LUS->>LUI: FHIR Webhook<br/>POST /alerts<br/>(FHIR Flag + linked Observation)
  Note over LUS,LUI: HMAC signature on payload<br/>+ optional Authorization header

  LUI->>CORE: Forward signal event<br/>{patient_id, alert_id,<br/>priority, observation_ref}
  CORE->>CORE: Pathway triggers<br/>(Notify clinician?)
  CORE->>BUS: Emit AlertReceived event

  par Write Observation + Flag to HiX
    BUS->>EHRI: Subscribe → outbound FHIR write
    EHRI->>HIX: POST Observation<br/>(BP reading, LOINC-coded,<br/>linked to Encounter)
    EHRI->>HIX: POST Flag<br/>(active, priority, period)
    HIX-->>EHRI: Resource IDs
  and Create clinician task
    BUS->>EHRI: Subscribe → task creation
    EHRI->>HIX: POST Task<br/>{patient, priority, due,<br/>focus=Flag, requester=platform}
    HIX-->>EHRI: Task ID
  and Patient-side guidance
    BUS->>LUI: Subscribe → patient guidance
    LUI->>LAPP: Push notification<br/>"Your reading is high —<br/>please rest 5 min and remeasure"
    LAPP-->>PT: Notification + content card
  and Audit
    BUS->>EHRI: Audit → Provenance<br/>(alert detection, severity,<br/>rule version)
    EHRI->>HIX: POST Provenance
  end
    Note over LUS,LUI: Todo - Missing the part where the <br/>main carepathway gets notified that <br/>there was an alert raised

  Note over HIX,CL: Task surfaces in the clinician's HiX task list.<br/>Clicking through SMART-launches the Luscii professional tools view<br/>with the alert in context (see Story 2).

  CL->>HIX: Open task in HiX worklist
  CL->>LUI: (via SMART launch, see Story 2)<br/>View alert + history
  LUI->>LUS: GET alert detail + trend
  LUS-->>LUI: Alert payload + 30-day trend
  LUI-->>CL: Render alert detail

  alt Clinician acknowledges + resolves
    CL->>LUI: Resolve alert<br/>(action: monitor / contact patient /<br/>escalate / refer)
    LUI->>LUS: Update Flag status → resolved<br/>(Class IIa-side state change)
    LUI->>CORE: Emit AlertResolved event
    CORE->>BUS: Forward → notification + audit
    par
      BUS->>EHRI: Update Flag in HiX (status=inactive)
      EHRI->>HIX: PUT Flag
    and
      BUS->>EHRI: Provenance: resolution
      EHRI->>HIX: POST Provenance
    end
  else Escalation needed
    CL->>LUI: Escalate
    LUI->>CORE: Trigger escalation pathway step<br/>(e.g. MDO, video consult, referral)
    Note over CORE,CL: See Story 5 (video consult) for downstream flows.
  end

  Note over PT,CL: The Luscii Clinical Engine is the only Class IIa component<br/>in the chain. Reaktor / Newwave components handle administrative<br/>orchestration only — never clinical decisions.